+- `generateReport` accepts optional `thresholds` argument to gate CI pipelines on metric scores.
+
+## Threshold Support
+- **CLI**: `frai eval --threshold <metric>=<min> --threshold <metric>=<min>` gates on metric scores (0–1 range).
+  - All thresholds pass → exit 0 (report written).
+  - Any threshold fails → exit 1 (report written with `passed: false`).
+  - Malformed input or unknown metric → exit 2 (no report).
+- **SDK**: `generateReport({ ..., thresholds: { exact_match: 0.9 } })` adds `passed` and `thresholds` fields to the report.
+  - Metrics without a score fail their threshold (instead of crashing).
+  - Custom metrics can be supplied to `runEvaluations` and referenced in thresholds if they define an `id` field.
+- **Reporting**: JSON reports gain `passed` and `thresholds` list; Markdown reports gain a "Thresholds" section.
 
